ondition and results of operations may be harmed.","block":458,"table":null,"attribution":"management","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001193125-26-076849","form":"10-K","filedAt":"2026-02-26","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001788999","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1788999/000119312526076849/xper-20251231.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/038885b28f8a208af85f0a2592427ff99e7965ca316c4128d4c6e5e3bce91042.bin","sha256":"038885b28f8a208af85f0a2592427ff99e7965ca316c4128d4c6e5e3bce91042"}},{"id":"87cc6cf403982a967a203fd4ecd03674c3bfc5b42020c130763ab5ba007710f1","quote":"We expect to derive a significant percentage of our revenue from the technologies, products, and services that we offer to manufacturers of consumer electronics products. We believe that demand for our audio technologies in growing markets for multi-channel and/or high-resolution audio, including TVs, tablets, mobile phones, video game consoles, automobiles, and soundbars, will be based on the amount, quality, and popularity of content (such as movies, TV shows, music, and games) either released in the DTS audio format or capable of being coded and played in the DTS format.","context":"We may not be able to maintain enough content released in the DTS audio format, which may reduce demand for our technologies, products, and services.","section":"has made the industry less predictable and more volatile and if we are unable to adapt to developments in this space, our business, financial condition and results of operations may be harmed.","block":459,"table":null,"attribution":"management","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001193125-26-076849","form":"10-K","filedAt":"2026-02-26","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001788999","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1788999/000119312526076849/xper-20251231.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/038885b28f8a208af85f0a2592427ff99e7965ca316c4128d4c6e5e3bce91042.b